{"instruction": "Context: Brute Force — 47 failed SSH logins from 185.220.101.0 against server WEB-01 in 3 minutes, followed by 1 successful login as user 'deploy'. OSINT: source IP is a known Tor exit node listed on 3 abuse feeds. UEBA: 'deploy' account never logs in from external IPs.", "output": "{"threat_type": "brute_force_success", "mitre_id": "T1110.001", "risk_score": 92, "risk_level": "critical", "analysis": "Password spraying followed by successful authentication from a Tor exit node. The 'deploy' service account has no history of external logins, indicating credential compromise. Immediate containment required before attacker establishes persistence.", "recommended_action": {"action_type": "block_ip_and_isolate", "target": "185.220.101.0 / WEB-01", "rationale": "Block source at FortiGate, isolate WEB-01, rotate deploy credentials, review post-auth commands"}, "predicted_next_move": "Attacker will likely attempt privilege escalation via sudo misconfigurations and install a persistence mechanism within the next hour.", "confidence": 0.94, "status": "pending"}", "incident_type": "brute_force"}
