{"instruction": "Context: Credential Dumping — Process 'mallory.exe' on DC-01 (192.168.56.100) opened LSASS handle with 0x1010 permissions. Hash of mallory.exe matches Mimikatz variant on VirusTotal (58/70). Event 4662: replication requests from non-DC account 'svc_backup'.", "output": "{"threat_type": "credential_dumping_dcsync", "mitre_id": "T1003.006", "risk_score": 98, "risk_level": "critical", "analysis": "Mimikatz execution on a domain controller combined with DCSync-style replication requests from a service account indicates domain-wide credential compromise. All domain credentials must be considered exposed. This is a domain takeover in progress.", "recommended_action": {"action_type": "isolate_host_and_reset_krbtgt", "target": "DC-01", "rationale": "Isolate DC-01, disable svc_backup, plan double krbtgt password reset, engage incident response for full AD recovery"}, "predicted_next_move": "Attacker already holds domain admin equivalent; expect Golden Ticket forging and deployment of ransomware staging within hours.", "confidence": 0.97, "status": "pending"}", "incident_type": "credential_access"}
{"instruction": "Context: Phishing — User marketing@corp.com clicked link in spoofed DocuSign email, redirected to login-corporate-verify.tk which captured SSO credentials. OSINT: domain registered 48h ago, resolves to 185.130.5.23 listed on 3 phishing feeds. Proxy log shows POST of credentials to the domain.", "output": "{"threat_type": "phishing_credential_theft", "mitre_id": "T1566.002", "risk_score": 88, "risk_level": "high", "analysis": "Confirmed credential capture via lookalike domain. Attacker possesses valid SSO credentials for a marketing user. Risk of immediate MFA-fatigue or session hijacking. Domain is fresh infrastructure typical of commodity phishing kits.", "recommended_action": {"action_type": "block_domain_and_reset_credentials", "target": "login-corporate-verify.tk / marketing@corp.com", "rationale": "Sinkhole domain at DNS, block IP 185.130.5.23 at FortiGate, force password reset + revoke sessions, sweep mail gateway for the same lure"}, "predicted_next_move": "Attacker will attempt login from residential proxy within minutes; watch for impossible-travel and MFA push fatigue.", "confidence": 0.93, "status": "pending"}", "incident_type": "phishing"}
{"instruction": "Context: Lateral Movement — WORKSTATION-23 (10.0.30.50) opened SMB sessions to 14 hosts in 4 minutes using NTLM auth of user 'helpdesk_svc'. Event 4624 type 3 spikes. helpdesk_svc normally touches max 3 hosts/day. EDR: psexec.exe copied to ADMIN$ on 6 targets.", "output": "{"threat_type": "lateral_movement_smb", "mitre_id": "T1021.002", "risk_score": 90, "risk_level": "critical", "analysis": "Service account credentials are being used for rapid SMB propagation with PsExec — classic worm-style lateral movement. 14 targets in 4 minutes far exceeds the behavioral baseline. Attacker likely holds helpdesk_svc hash via Pass-the-Hash.", "recommended_action": {"action_type": "isolate_hosts_and_disable_account", "target": "WORKSTATION-23 + 14 SMB targets / helpdesk_svc", "rationale": "Isolate source host, disable helpdesk_svc, block ADMIN$ shares at FortiGate, deploy emergency EDR scan on all 14 targets"}, "predicted_next_move": "Next targets will be domain controllers and backup servers for credential harvesting and ransomware staging.", "confidence": 0.95, "status": "pending"}", "incident_type": "lateral_movement"}
